From 97956f05b2737b746dc9ca9b59f99174f42f9310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Truls Asheim <truls@asheim.dk>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 14:26:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: networking operations retry on timeout

This patch adds a configurable retry mechanism to the kms-pkcs11
signing module to handle frequent timeout errors from AWS.

The environment variable AWS_KMS_PKCS11_RETRIES controls how
many times a KMS signing operation is retried after a curl timeout. It
defaults to 10; set it to 0 to disable these retries. When debug
logging is enabled, every signing attempt is reported.

Signed-off-by: Truls Asheim <truls@squaremind.io>
Upstream-status: Pending
